From ec7456253249d6b3c07a7b239d79896e48bf2c65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:54:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(multiaxis): refuse a work-turning rotary line off the WCS
 origin

The index-swing clause and the posed first-traverse law read each
work-turning rotary line through the WCS origin. A stated non-zero
pivot or offset moves the line, and the project cannot place it in
the WCS. Both clauses now refuse such a rotary by name. A zero pivot
or offset is judged as before; a lone vertical line keeps every
height and is not refused.

Fixes #3127

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
